Z||000000||SteveJ||10-31-2001||11:28 AM||||I love games at Osama's expense BUT:<P>If you have run the game program, "Yo Mama, Osama"  which claims to raise<BR>money for the American Red Cross you probably have a Trojan in your machine.<BR>It is not destructive but is spyware and will slow down your machine with<BR>it's internet access. Go to this site for explanation and remedy. <A HREF="http://antivirus.about.com/library/weekly/aa101701b.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://antivirus.about.com/library/weekly/aa101701b.htm</A> <P>AS instructed Press CTRL-ALT-DEL and use the Task Manager find WNAD.EXE if<BR>it is running on your machine. If so use "End Task" to force the close of<BR>WNAD.EXE.   This must be done first then the files deleted.<P>The files WNAD.EXE, WNAD.DAT are located in the c:\windows subdirectory. The<BR>file WNAD.LGC  is in the C:\windows\applog subdirectory.<P>All three of these files should be deleted.<P>I did not find the file WNAD-UPDATE.EXE in my machine. You should do a find<BR>files on that name to see if it needs deleting on yours.<P>If you are uncomfortable editing your registry don't worry about it. Once<BR>the files are gone the program can't run and the attempt to start it when<BR>windows starts will simply fail harmlessly.<P>( Incidentally it was Zone Alarm that alerted me to the fact that I had this problem when the program attempted to access the internet. )<P>( <A HREF="http://www.twistedhumor.com" TARGET=_blank>www.twistedhumor.com</A>  is now in the same category as EdsB52 )||||reg||1
